cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this release, please cite this work and the upstream PROTAC-DB 3.0 source database."
title: "Bias-Aware Learning from Censored and Incompletely Observed PROTAC Degradation Data: Dataset and Code"
type: software
version: 1.0.2
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Guanglu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8693-1923"
    affiliation: "College of Computer Science and Technology / Qingdao Institute of Software, China University of Petroleum (East China)"
  - family-names: "Wang"
    given-names: "Shuang"
    affiliation: "College of Computer Science and Technology / Qingdao Institute of Software, China University of Petroleum (East China)"
    email: "wangshuang@upc.edu.cn"
repository-code: "https://github.com/liuguang-jpt/release"
# The version-specific Zenodo DOI will be added after the v1.0.2 deposition is published and verified.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Public GitHub release containing project-authored code and documentation for a
  bias-aware PROTAC degradation benchmark, PROTAC-DB-derived analysis artefacts,
  a 150-record calibration annotation set, a 132-record adjudicated
  internal-consistency sample, frozen grouped split manifests, and aggregate
  TPDdb-derived external-evaluation outputs. The internal-consistency sample is
  not independent expert validation. Record-level PROTAC-DB-derived materials
  remain subject to upstream terms; raw PROTAC-DB snapshots and TPDdb-derived
  record-level cohorts, labels and predictions are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - PROTAC
  - targeted protein degradation
  - positive-unlabeled learning
  - censored data
  - label bias
  - calibration
  - grouped validation
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
  - external validation
